# Training runs.
#
# Run data is large (~28 TB) and machine-generated, so it never enters git.
# Its WRITE-UPS do: NOTES.md is the analysis of a run and the only place its
# numbers and argument live, and the archive READMEs say why an invalidated
# run cannot be cited. PROCESS.md treats both as canonical, and STATE.md
# cites them. Everything else under runs/ -- checkpoints, traces, metrics,
# figures, the .csv the reports link to -- stays local.
runs/**
!runs/**/
!runs/**/*.md
slurm_scripts/
slurm_logs/
data/

# Model weights and HuggingFace cache
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.ggml
.cache/

